            category: "Apple cultivars for southern Wisconsin",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Fruit ripens in early October.",
            description: "With an intense sweet, aromatic flavor, the small red apple is great for drying (chips) and cider. Storage life is about three months. The trees are very winter-hardy, moderately vigorous, and spreading. Fruit ripens in early October"
