        {
            type: "Apple",
            name: "Cortland",
            category: "Apple cultivars for southern Wisconsin",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Fruit ripens in late September.",
            description: "A McIntosh offspring with very good quality fruit. The tender flesh is slow to brown, and the tangy-sweet flavor is good for fresh use and baking. This annual bearing tree has a weeping, willowy growth habit. It is winter-hardy, but is susceptible to apple scab. Red sports such as Redcort and Royalcort are similar, but the fruit ripens earlier and the trees have shorter lifespans. Fruit ripens in late September"
        },
        {
