            category: "Apple cultivars for southern Wisconsin",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Fruit ripens in late August.",
            description: "This red, McIntosh-type apple has excellent flavor for fresh use. Fruit only lasts in storage for two to three weeks at most. The trees are very large and susceptible to fire blight and scab. Fruit ripens in late August"
